From 85f98ddc2d07837f859b7ade3cb89ae3b6376207 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Buildroot Demo <buildroot-demo@example.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbv: clear framebuffer before each image

fbv only overwrites the rectangle occupied by the current image. When two
aspect-preserving images have different shapes, pixels outside the new image
therefore retain parts of the previous slide.

Clear the mapped framebuffer to black before every blit. This gives each
image clean letterbox or pillarbox bars and also gives transparent image
regions a predictable background. Keep this independent of --dontclear,
which controls terminal escape sequences and must remain enabled so fbv does
not erase the serial console.
---
 fb_display.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/fb_display.c
+++ b/fb_display.c
@@ -223,6 +223,8 @@ void blit2FB(int fh, void *fbbuff, unsig
 		return;
 	}
 
+	memset(fb, 0, scr_xs * scr_ys * cpp);
+
 	if(cpp == 1)
 	{
 	    get8map(fh, &map_back);
